    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ87YE9M4",
      "title": "feat(op-conductor-ops): migrate to apko + melange",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 615,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nMigrate `op-conductor-ops` from a hand-written `python:3.12-slim-bookworm` Dockerfile to a declarative apko + melange build using upstream Wolfi packages and the factory `apko.yaml` reusable workflow.\n\nThe Dockerfile was previously running \\`poetry install\\` inside the container at **runtime** (every container start), and the launcher script ran a fresh \\`poetry install\\` again. With apko, every dependency is resolved at build time as a signed Wolfi apk, the wheel is built via PEP 517 (\\`python -m build\\` → installer), and the main container has no shell, no poetry, and no pip.\n\n## Project changes\n\n- Move flat-file Python modules into a proper \\`op_conductor_ops/\\` package directory; convert sibling imports (\\`from network import …\\`) to relative (\\`from .network import …\\`).\n- Wrap the typer entrypoint in a \\`main()\\` function so it can be registered as a \\`[tool.poetry.scripts]\\` entry.\n- Update \\`pyproject.toml\\`:\n    - Drop \\`package-mode = false\\`.\n    - Add \\`version = \"0.0.1\"\\` and \\`packages = [{ include = \"op_conductor_ops\" }]\\`.\n    - Register the \\`op-conductor-ops\\` console script at \\`op_conductor_ops.cli:main\\`.\n- Drop the legacy shell launcher that ran \\`poetry install\\` at container startup. apko-built images install everything at build time.\n\n## Build changes\n\n- Add \\`op-conductor-ops/melange.yaml\\`. One pipeline step: \\`uses: python/build-wheel\\`. The PEP 517 frontend reads \\`pyproject.toml\\` and invokes \\`poetry-core\\` to produce a wheel. The runtime closure is declared via Wolfi apk names mirroring \\`[tool.poetry.dependencies]\\`.\n- Add \\`op-conductor-ops/apko/op-conductor-ops.apko.yaml\\`. Pulls \\`wolfi-baselayout\\`, \\`ca-certificates-bundle\\`, \\`tzdata\\`, and the melange-produced \\`op-conductor-ops\\` apk. Runs as uid 65532 (non-root).\n- Update \\`.github/images.json\\`: add \\`op-conductor-ops\\` as a \\`groups\\` entry (\\`mode: apko\\`, \\`services: [op-conductor-ops]\\`) and remove it from the Dockerfile-mode \\`images\\` map.\n- Update \\`branches.yaml\\` + \\`tags.yaml\\`: replace the legacy \\`detect-changes\\` / \\`parse-tag\\` actions with \\`factory/actions/plan\\` and add a job that calls \\`factory/.github/workflows/apko.yaml\\` for the \\`op-conductor-ops\\` group.\n\n## Verified locally\n\n\\`\\`\\`\n$ docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 op-conductor-ops:apko-test-amd64 --help\n Usage: op-conductor-ops [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...\n CLI for managing OP Conductor sequencers.\n   ...\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nImage rebuilt cleanly with no manual fiddling. melange's SCA emitted the runtime closure auto-detected from the wheel's METADATA file (no manual \\`pip install\\` step needed).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Branch CI: factory \\`plan\\` action emits \\`op-conductor-ops\\` under \\`groups_matrix_json\\`; \\`apko.yaml\\` reusable workflow runs and publishes \\`us-docker.pkg.dev/oplabs-tools-artifacts/images/op-conductor-ops:<branch>\\`\n- [ ] Smoke test passes: \\`op-conductor-ops --version\\` returns successfully\n- [ ] Tag push (\\`op-conductor-ops/v<semver>\\`) builds and publishes the same image at the version tag\n- [ ] Existing Dockerfile-mode images (cci-stats, op-acceptor, etc.) keep building unchanged via the \\`local\\` matrix job\n\n## Pattern\n\nThis PR is the first apko migration in this repo. The \\`groups\\` shape in \\`.github/images.json\\` plus the dedicated job in \\`branches.yaml\\` is intended to be reused for subsequent migrations — one group entry + one job per migrated image (or one group with multiple services if they share a melange config).",
